Description: soft ISP: gentler auto exposure and white balance
 On the POCO X3 NFC (Mobian) the soft ISP's grey-world white balance turned a
 lamp-lit room blue-white and a yellow floor blue, and with a fresh estimate on
 every frame the colours jumped on a noisy picture; the exposure aimed for the
 middle of the range, which came out washed out after the gamma curve, and
 chased the noise in 15 % steps (flicker). White balance now corrects 65 % of
 the way with a slight warm bias and moves 15 % per frame towards the new
 estimate; exposure aims a little lower in steps of at most 6 %. When the
 sensor is at its longest exposure and highest gain and the picture is still
 dark, the ISP adds up to 4x digital gain (on the colour gains) and takes it
 back first when the picture gets too bright.
Author: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
